preConditionHook:
// After N consecutive losing closed trades, stand down for M bars from the
// last exit. Measured accessors only (positionprofit/totaltrades and
// barssinceexit rows): PositionProfit(k) is the k-th most recently closed
// position net of the full round turn and 0.0 when fewer than k have closed
// (so a short history can never count as a streak); BarsSinceExit(1) is 0 on
// the exit's fill bar and counts up. The streak is "all of the last N closed
// positions lost", counted with a loop because EL has no streak word.
//
// NOT A LATCH: the cooldown runs off BarsSinceExit, which keeps counting
// while the Switch holds the strategy flat, so trading resumes after M bars.
// A further loss re-arms it; a win breaks the streak. lossCount must be >= 1:
// at 0 the streak test is always true and, before any exit, BarsSinceExit
// stays 0, which would block the strategy for good. A reversal that closes
// the N-th loser re-opens a position on the same fill; the Switch afterwards
// flattens it at the next open, in both twins.
lossStreak = 0;
for (int k = 1; k <= (int)lossCount; ++k) {
    if (el_lt(ctx.PositionProfit(k), 0.0)) lossStreak = lossStreak + 1;
}
